# Two UV-mapped quads for the patterns golden. Written by hand rather than
# exported: every other mesh here has no `vt` lines at all, and a scene that is
# about texture coordinates needs a surface that has some.
#
# Both are wound so their geometric normal faces the room — the wall emits, and
# emission is one-sided.

# Floor, y = 0, twelve units square, facing +y.
v -6.0 0.0 -6.0
v -6.0 0.0  6.0
v  6.0 0.0  6.0
v  6.0 0.0 -6.0

# Wall, z = -6, twelve wide and eight high, facing +z.
v -6.0 0.0 -6.0
v  6.0 0.0 -6.0
v  6.0 8.0 -6.0
v -6.0 8.0 -6.0

# The unit square, shared by both: u runs left to right across each quad, v runs
# away from the camera on the floor and upward on the wall.
vt 0.0 0.0
vt 0.0 1.0
vt 1.0 1.0
vt 1.0 0.0

o Floor
f 1/1 2/2 3/3 4/4

o Wall
f 5/1 6/4 7/3 8/2
